**/.terraform*
**/terraform.tfstate*
**/Dockerfile.*
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/*
**/.DS_Store
logs/*
.env
*.log
aloasi.txt
eks-cluster/terraform/aws-eks-cluster-and-nodegroup/terraform.tfvars
eks-cluster/terraform/**/backend.tf
/shelf/
/workspace.xml
# Editor-based HTTP Client requests
/httpRequests/
# Environment-dependent path to Maven home directory
/mavenHomeManager.xml
# Datasource local storage ignored files
/dataSources/
/dataSources.local.xml
/.idea/*
/docs/eks-agent.md
.claude/

# Terraform variable files are not committed, templates included. They pin a region, a set of
# AZs and a cluster name, and the bucket names they reference commonly carry the AWS account ID
# -- none of which belongs in a public fork, and all of which is wrong for anyone else's account.
# Keep working copies outside any checkout (~/clusters/<cluster>/) and document the *choices* in
# a README rather than shipping a file that hardcodes them.
#
# `*.tfvars` does not match `foo.tfvars.example`, hence the second pattern. The two upstream
# terraform.tfvars.example files predate this rule and are left tracked deliberately: they are
# not ours to remove, and the negations below keep them working.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.example
!eks-cluster/terraform/aws-eks-cluster-and-nodegroup/terraform.tfvars.example
!examples/agentic/aws-devops-agent-workshop/terraform/terraform.tfvars.example

# Per-cluster environment files (TF_VAR_* exports, bucket names)
env.sh
*.env
